      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-136446",
      ":question/problem": "The height of a tide at a particular harbor, in meters, can be modeled by the function\n$H(t) = 3\\sin (\\frac{\u03c0t}{6}) + 4$,\nwhere $t$ is the time (in hours) after $12p.m$. What is the height difference between high tide and low tide?"
